---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = "The Geriatrician's Guide — Senior Living Guidance from a Stanford-Trained Geriatrician";
const description = "Clinical clarity for people facing senior living decisions. Free tools, physician-written guidance, and no placement commissions. Ever.";
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>

<section class="hero" data-screen-label="Hero">
<div class="hero__inner">
<div class="hero__text">
<h1>An insider&rsquo;s view of senior care, from a geriatrician with no agenda but yours.</h1>
<p class="hero__sub">Free tools and a complete guide for deciding when a loved one needs more care, where they should live, and how to pay for it. Written by a Stanford-trained, board-certified physician who has spent years caring for patients in senior living communities. Everything here puts my experience in your hands, to empower you to make the decisions that matter most.</p>
<div class="hero__cta">
<a class="btn btn--outline" href="/is-it-time">Take the Is It Time? assessment <svg width="17" height="17" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></a>
<a class="hero__more" href="#free-tools">or see all the free tools&nbsp;&darr;</a>
</div>
</div>
<figure class="hero__figure">
<div class="hero__media"><img src="/images/hero-genualdi.png" alt="Dr. Michael D. Genualdi, MD, board-certified geriatrician" width="1264" height="848"></div>
<figcaption class="hero__caption"><a class="hero__caption-link" href="/about">Michael D. Genualdi, MD</a><br><span class="hero__caption-sub">Board-certified in Geriatrics &amp; Internal Medicine</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</div>
</section>
<section class="independence" data-screen-label="Independence">
<div class="independence__inner">
<div class="independence__rule"></div>
<h2 class="independence__claim">No placement commissions. No facility money. Ever.</h2>
<p class="independence__support">Placement services are paid by the communities they recommend. I built this to be one voice in the process with nothing to gain from where your loved one moves.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section class="stages" id="free-tools" data-screen-label="Stages">
<div class="stages__inner">
<div class="stages__head">
<h2>Free guidance for whatever stage of the road you&rsquo;re on</h2>
</div>
<div class="stages__grid">
<article class="stage"><span class="stage__n">01</span><h3>Is it time?</h3><p>Safety, daily tasks, and caregiver strain, scored against the signs I look for in clinic.</p><ul><li><span>Free assessment</span><a href="/is-it-time">Is It Time?</a></li></ul></article>
<article class="stage"><span class="stage__n">02</span><h3>Start the conversation</h3><p>How to raise a move with your loved one and your siblings without it becoming an ultimatum.</p><ul><li><span>Free guide</span><a href="/starting-the-conversation">Starting the Conversation</a></li></ul></article>
<article class="stage"><span class="stage__n">03</span><h3>Tour communities</h3><p>What to ask, what to watch for, and how to compare communities after the visits blur together.</p><ul><li><span>Free kit &middot; 4 printable tools</span><a href="/tour-kit">Tour Day Kit</a></li></ul></article>
<article class="stage"><span class="stage__n">04</span><h3>Check the medications</h3><p>The nine-step review I run with every new patient, and one list for every prescription and supplement.</p><ul><li><span>Free kit &middot; 2 printable tools</span><a href="/medication-audit">Medication Audit Kit</a></li></ul></article>
</div>
<p class="stages__bridge">These cover one decision at a time. <em>The Long Road</em> puts every stage in order, start to finish.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section class="teaser" data-screen-label="Product teaser">
<div class="teaser__inner">
<div class="teaser__text">
<p class="teaser__eyebrow">The Flagship</p>
<h2 class="teaser__title">The Long Road</h2>
<p class="teaser__sub">A Geriatrician&rsquo;s Complete Guide to Senior Care Decisions</p>
<p class="teaser__body">Forty-one chapters covering all four stages, from the first signs of decline through end-of-life decisions. The finances, the tour, the contract, the conversation no one wants to start. Written for anyone deciding this for someone they love.</p>
<p class="teaser__price">$97 &middot; Instant download</p>
<div class="teaser__actions">
<a class="btn btn--primary" href="/the-long-road">Buy the book <svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></a>
<a class="btn btn--ghost-ink" href="/the-long-road#fc-form">Read Chapter 11 free</a>
</div>
</div>
<figure class="teaser__figure"><img src="/images/the-long-road-cover.png" alt="The Long Road — A Geriatrician's Complete Guide to Senior Care Decisions, by Michael D. Genualdi, MD" width="2474" height="3200"></figure>
</div>
</section>
<section class="insider" data-screen-label="Authority bridge">
<div class="insider__inner">
<div class="insider__head"><h2 class="insider__title">I know what a well&#8209;run community looks like from the inside.</h2><a class="textlink" href="/about">About Dr. Genualdi <svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></a></div>
<figure class="insider__inset"><p class="insider__eyebrow">What I see when I walk in</p><blockquote><p>The lobby tells you nothing about whether your money (or your loved one) is safe. I&rsquo;ve walked into beautiful communities and known after my first visit that something was wrong &mdash; staff stretched thin, corners being cut, a gap between the promise the building made and the reality of how it operated. The communities I&rsquo;d want my own loved ones in weren&rsquo;t always the most glamorous ones. They were the ones where the money was clearly going into the care: enough staff, consistent faces, a culture that felt unhurried. Nurses and aides who communicated clearly, carried out orders reliably, and had the clinical judgment to recognize when something wasn&rsquo;t right and act on it. A new fountain in the lobby is easy. That kind of staffing is hard, and it&rsquo;s what actually matters.</p></blockquote><figcaption>From Chapter 17 of <cite>The Long Road</cite></figcaption></figure>
</div>
</section>
<section class="blog-teaser" data-screen-label="Blog teaser">
<div class="blog-teaser__inner">
<p class="blog-teaser__eyebrow">From the Guide</p>
<h2 class="blog-teaser__title">Recent articles</h2>
<p class="blog-teaser__intro">Physician-written notes on the questions that come up most on tours, in contracts, and in the room with your loved one.</p>
<div class="blog-teaser__grid">
<article class="blog-teaser__card"><a class="blog-teaser__card-title" href="/blog/assisted-living-contract-questions">Five Questions to Ask Before Signing an Assisted Living Contract</a><p class="blog-teaser__card-meta">July 7, 2026</p><p class="blog-teaser__card-desc">Most people sign assisted living contracts without reading the arbitration clause. Here is what a geriatrician looks for before anyone signs.</p></article>
<article class="blog-teaser__card"><a class="blog-teaser__card-title" href="/blog/memory-care-staffing-question">The One Staffing Question Nobody Asks on a Memory Care Tour</a><p class="blog-teaser__card-meta">June 23, 2026</p><p class="blog-teaser__card-desc">What is posted on the wall and what is staffed at 11 PM on a Tuesday are two different numbers. A geriatrician explains how to get the real one.</p></article>
</div>
<a class="textlink" href="/blog">Read all articles <svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></a>
</div>
</section>

</BaseLayout>
